<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">

<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
  <title>Organizer FAQ | Platform</title>
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="/css/styles.css">
  <link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Inter:wght@300;400;500;600;700&display=swap" rel="stylesheet">
  <style>
    .faq-container {
      max-width: 800px;
      margin: 4rem auto;
      padding: 2rem;
    }

    .faq-item {
      background: var(--card-bg);
      border: 1px solid var(--border-color);
      padding: 1.5rem;
      margin-bottom: 1rem;
      border-radius: 12px;
    }

    .faq-question {
      font-weight: 600;
      font-size: 1.2rem;
      color: #fff;
      margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
    }

    .faq-answer {
      color: var(--text-muted);
      line-height: 1.6;
    }

    .faq-highlight {
      color: var(--accent-gold);
      font-weight: 600;
    }
  </style>
</head>

<body>
  <%- include('partials/header') %>

    <div class="faq-container">
      <h1 style="text-align: center; margin-bottom: 1rem; color: white;">Organizer FAQ</h1>
      <p style="text-align: center; color: var(--text-muted); margin-bottom: 3rem;">
        Empowering competition organizers with unparalleled digital reach and brand visibility.
      </p>

      <div class="faq-item">
        <div class="faq-question">Why should I upload my results here instead of just my website?</div>
        <div class="faq-answer">
          When you upload your results to our platform, they are permanently linked to the <span
            class="faq-highlight">digital portfolios of thousands of dancers and studios</span>. Instead of data/PDF
          that might get lost over time, your awards become dynamic trophies that dancers share on social media, use for
          college recruiting, and embed on their studio websites—giving your organization unprecedented, ongoing brand
          visibility. At the minumum, we serve as a free backup for your award data, and extra visibility for your
          organization.
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="faq-item">
        <div class="faq-question">How does custom branding work?</div>
        <div class="faq-answer">
          When you claim your Organizer profile, you gain access to a powerful set of branding tools. First, you can set
          a custom <span class="faq-highlight">Slogan and Event Description</span> to market your competition directly
          on your public page on our site.
          <br><br>
          Second, you can upload your official logo. Using our interactive display sliders, you can set the size and
          transparency of your logo — then our design team hand-fits it onto the "Trophy Cards" displayed on dancer
          portfolios before it goes live, so every card your dancers share looks polished, usually within a day or two.
          <br><br>
          Finally, you can upload specific <span class="faq-highlight">Custom Trophy Icons</span> mapped precisely to
          your award taxonomy. Want a Crown icon for Title Winners and a Diamond for Platinum adjudication? You can
          configure it all, completely replacing our default icons and turning every award won at your event into an
          enduring personalized advertisement for your competition.
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="faq-item">
        <div class="faq-question">What file formats are supported for upload?</div>
        <div class="faq-answer">
          You can upload standard <span class="faq-highlight">.CSV</span> or <span class="faq-highlight">.XLSX
            (Excel)</span> files directly from your scoring system — but we also accept
          <span class="faq-highlight">PDFs and database exports</span>: SQL dumps (MySQL, PostgreSQL), SQLite or
          Access files, or a ZIP of any of these, up to 50&nbsp;MB per upload (contact us for anything larger).
          Once uploaded, our team will parse the data, verify it, and seamlessly integrate it into the dancer and
          studio portfolios.
          <br><br>
          Any layout works, but your results go live fastest when each row includes the
          <span class="faq-highlight">event name and date, routine name, placement, category or style, age division,
            dancer name(s), and studio</span>. Full dancer names (rather than initials) and consistent studio
          spellings help us match records correctly on the first pass. A ready-made CSV template is available on the
          <span class="faq-highlight">Upload Results</span> tab of your dashboard — a brand-new account opens straight onto it, with a three-step setup checklist (upload results, marketing profile, logo) guiding the rest.
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- <div class="faq-item">
        <div class="faq-question">How do the analytics help my organization?</div>
        <div class="faq-answer">
          Your dashboard provides deep demographic insights that you can't get anywhere else. We track the performance
          of studios across the country. You can see various information, such as geographic heatmaps, to help you
          decide where to expand your tour next season.
        </div>
      </div> -->

      <div class="faq-item">
        <div class="faq-question">Can I link my registration portal?</div>
        <div class="faq-answer">
          Yes! On your verified historical results pages, we can embed a prominent "Register for Next Year" button. This
          captures dancers and studio owners right when they are checking their results and are most engaged with your
          brand.
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="faq-item">
        <div class="faq-question">What is the "Presented by" page on award cards?</div>
        <div class="faq-answer">
          Award cards can flip into a mini-book, and the closing page is your colophon: your approved logo shown
          large, your organization's name, and an optional one-line tagline (set it on your Branding page under
          "Card 'Presented by' Tagline"). It appears on every card from your events once our design team has fitted
          and approved your logo — your brand on every card dancers share, including the flip side.
        </div>
      </div>

    </div>
</body>

</html>